  "description": "A new forecast is setting off alarms for the market",
  "body_html": "<p>“Are we still getting a rate cut?!” was a question in the chat today. And when I checked the recently updated forecasts, the alarms were going off in my head. We can talk about that more shortly…</p><p>Another common comment I am seeing is: “I got stopped out too soon!” or worse…getting stopped out initially and taking a loss. Let me be clear: there is no perfect method to stops, it will happen on occasion, and I personally understand your frustration. However, we can reduce how often we are stopped out, especially as we first enter into a trade. I always evaluate the market cap before entering into a trade. Think about it…are you going to trade a meme stock the same way you do the S&amp;P 500? Of course not. </p><p>You can check out the article that is packed with free to use tools and indicators I personally built, in the article <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/90-of-traders-fail-and-100-of-them?r=4z8lgl\">90% of traders Fail, and 100% of them all use the same indicators…SO DON’T!</a> In that article, you will find the Market Cap Move Estimator, and a link to a TradingView tool. Add that tool to your favorites, and ensure you update the market cap in the settings, but you can see what an “average” day looks like for the stock you are trading. </p><p>For example, Rigetti with a $5.6B market cap, can move on average 8.6% in a single day. Whereas a larger company like Walmart has a $805B market cap, an average move for it is 2.4%. Clearly, you are going to need looser stops with smaller market cap companies. You reduce risk to your portfolio equity by starting with a smaller position initially, and then adding to the position when and if it begins to trend the direction you speculated. </p><p>As always, if you have questions feel free to ping me in the chat about it. I’m always happy to take a look at what you are trading if you want a 2nd, NFA opinion. </p><p>Now…about those rate cuts…⬇️</p><p><em>Subscribers get direct access with me Monday to Friday during market hours in the chat, stock reviews and access to our StockTok Dashboard, updated daily. <strong><a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe\">Subscribe Now.</a></strong></em></p>",
